# BuildKit per-Dockerfile ignore.
#
# The 1.1 GB .venv is the one that matters: the Dockerfile ends with `COPY . `,
# so without this the whole venv (plus .git) ships to the daemon and lands in the
# image. data/ is deliberately NOT excluded — the source PDFs (~4.3 MB) are baked
# into the image on purpose.
#
# Excluding **/.env is hygiene here, not load-bearing: build_index.py uses plain
# load_dotenv (no override=True), so the compose-injected DATABASE_URL=db:5432
# already wins over any baked .env. We still drop it to keep the context lean and
# match the sibling repos.
**/.venv
**/.git
**/__pycache__
**/.env
**/*.md
